content.text:
Interesting: the unresolved-key scan passed even though app.slint now doesn't yet reference new keys; that's fine. But after I add keys to apply_language and app.slint, the scan may check literal keys exist — they do.

Now update main.rs apply_language to set show/hide/remove-rule. Add after `set_import_from_excel`:

```rust
s.set_show_details(text(lang, "common.showDetails").into());
s.set_hide_details(text(lang, "common.hideDetails").into());
s.set_remove_rule(text(lang, "settings.removeRule").into());
```

Then app.slint.

Now design app.slint changes:

1. Add structs:
```slint
export struct HoldItem {
    id: string,
    status: string,
}

export struct PendingRuleItem {
    rule-type: string,
    key: string,
    value: string,
}
```
Note Slint struct property names with hyphen? In existing structs they use plain names. For consistency use `rule_type`? Slint identifiers allow `-` in property names? Slint uses `-` as separator in property names (e.g. `in-out property <string> policy-error`). For struct fields, examples use `owner`, `name`. I'll use `rule-type` and access in Rust as `rule_type` (Slint generates snake_case). Actually existing generated Rust for `ProfileItem` has `owner`, etc. For hyphenated fields, Slint's Rust binding converts `-` to `_`. That's standard. But to be safe and consistent, maybe name field `ruleType`? Slint converts camelCase? Let me avoid ambiguity: use `rule-type` — Slint docs show structs with `property <int> my-property;` and Rust getter `my_property`. Yes.

2. Strings additions:
```slint
in-out property <string> show-details;
in-out property <string> hide-details;
in-out property <string> remove-rule;
```

3. AppWindow properties:
```slint
in-out property <[HoldItem]> legal-holds: [];
in-out property <[PendingRuleItem]> pending-rules: [];
in-out property <string> policy-evaluation-detail: "";
in-out property <bool> policy-evaluation-detail-visible: false;
in-out property <string> legal-hold-release-reason-input: "";
```

4. Callbacks:
```slint
callback remove-policy-rule(int);
callback toggle-policy-evaluation-detail();
callback select-legal-hold(string);
```

5. UI:
- Fix nav buttons for Settings/Profiles to call select-page.
- Pending rules list: after the "rules pending" row, add:
```slint
for rule[index] in root.pending-rules: HorizontalLayout {
    spacing: 8px;
    Text { text: rule.rule-type + " · " + rule.key + " = " + rule.value; ... }
    Button { text: Strings.remove-rule; clicked => { root.remove-policy-rule(index); } }
}
```
Slint `for x[index] in model:` syntax is supported (since 1.x). Yes.

- Evaluation detail: after policy-status Text:
```slint
if root.policy-evaluation-detail != "": VerticalLayout {
    spacing: 4px;
    Button {
        text: root.policy-evaluation-detail-visible ? Strings.hide-details : Strings.show-details;
        clicked => { root.toggle-policy-evaluation-detail(); }
    }
    if root.policy-evaluation-detail-visible: Text {
        text: root.policy-evaluation-detail;
        color: Theme.text;
        wrap: word-wrap;
        font-family: "monospace";
    }
}
```
Does Slint Text support `font-family`? Yes, `font-family` property.

- Legal holds list: after heading/error, before inputs:
```slint
for hold in root.legal-holds: HorizontalLayout {
    spacing: 8px;
    Text { text: hold.id + " · " + hold.status; ... }
    Button { text: Strings.view-button; clicked => { root.select-legal-hold(hold.id); } }
}
```
If list empty show no-data? optional.

- Release reason input under selected hold:
```slint
if root.legal-hold-can-release: VerticalLayout {
    spacing: 6px;
    LineEdit {
        placeholder-text: Strings.reason-placeholder;
        text <=> root.legal-hold-release-reason-input;
    }
    Button {
        text: Strings.release-button;
        enabled: root.legal-hold-release-reason-input != "";
        clicked => { root.release-legal-hold(); }
    }
}
```

Now, `policy-evaluation-detail` pretty JSON with newlines in Text: Slint Text renders `\n`? I believe Slint Text supports multi-line text with `\n`. Yes.

Potential Slint issue: `for rule[index] in root.pending-rules` — index variable syntax. Slint supports `for item[index] in model`. Good.

Also `rule.rule-type` access — Slint field named `rule-type` accessed as `rule.rule-type`. Good.

